  "details": "\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: undefined behavior\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27766.patch: fix undefined behavior\n       in the form of values outside the range of 'unsigned long' type.\n     - CVE-2020-27766\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: division by zero\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2021-*.patch: fix potential division by zero\n       in many places.\n     - CVE-2021-20176, CVE-2021-20241, CVE-2021-20243,\n       CVE-2021-20244, CVE-2021-20246, CVE-2021-20309,\n       CVE-2021-20311\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: integer overflow\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2021-20312.patch: fix potential integer overflow\n       in coders/thumbnail.c which can affect system availability.\n     - CVE-2021-20312\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: data leak\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2021-20313.patch: ensure memory is always zeroed\n       in magick/memory.c.\n     - CVE-2021-20313",
